  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1009.01 High Risk Driver",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1009.01 High Risk Driver. For the purposes of this section, \"high risk driver\" means a driver who, because of an apparent physical or psychological impairment or condition, needs a reexamination in order to determine their fitness to safely drive a motor vehicle so as not to endanger the public.\n\nSource. #8109, eff 6-24-04; ss by #10176, eff 8-23-12; ss by #13685, eff 8-5-23 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Saf-C 1000)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1000.html"
